  "faq": [
    {
      "question": "What is the average cost of dining out in Malmö?",
      "answer": "The average cost varies widely depending on the type of restaurant. A casual lunch or a dish from a food hall can range from SEK 100-200 ($9-18). A mid-range dinner with drinks typically costs SEK 300-500 ($28-47) per person, while fine dining experiences, especially tasting menus, can start from SEK 800 ($75) and go much higher."
    },
    {
      "question": "Do I need to make reservations for restaurants in Malmö?",
      "answer": "For popular and highly-rated restaurants, especially during peak dinner hours and on weekends, reservations are strongly recommended, sometimes even essential weeks in advance for Michelin-starred venues. For casual eateries, reservations are often not required, but it's always a good idea to check their website or call ahead."
    },
    {
      "question": "Are vegetarian and vegan options readily available in Malmö?",
      "answer": "Yes, Malmö is very vegetarian and vegan-friendly. Many restaurants offer specific plant-based options, and there are also dedicated vegetarian/vegan eateries. The food hall, Malmö Saluhall, and places like Laziza (Lebanese buffet) often have excellent selections. Just look for 'vegetarisk' or 'vegansk' on menus."
    },
    {
      "question": "What local dishes should I try in Malmö?",
      "answer": "Beyond classic Swedish meatballs, don't miss Malmö's take on Falafel (often considered some of the best in Sweden), 'Äggakaka' (a thick, fluffy egg pancake served with fried pork and lingonberries), and fresh seafood from the Oresund region. In autumn, look for dishes featuring locally foraged mushrooms and game."
    },
    {
      "question": "Is tipping customary in Malmö restaurants?",
      "answer": "Tipping is not mandatory in Sweden, as service charges are usually included in the price. However, it's common to round up the bill or leave a small tip (5-10%) for excellent service, especially in nicer restaurants. It's always appreciated but never expected."
    },
    {
      "question": "What areas in Malmö are best for dining out?",
      "answer": "Malmö offers diverse dining experiences across its neighborhoods. Gamla Väster is excellent for upscale and modern European cuisine, while Möllevången (Möllan) is known for its vibrant international food scene and casual eateries. Davidshall offers trendy spots, and Västra Hamnen provides modern restaurants with often stunning waterfront views."
    }
